# Dashboard theme A′ (purple frame + light surfaces)

Vuetify `defaultTheme` is **light**. Product decision (2026-09-05): keep `App.vue` purple canvas; tab **content** uses light surfaces (`--surface-bg`). See wiki `dashboard-theme-improvement-plan.md`.

## Rules

- **New tab content**: white/light gray card on purple canvas. No full-page `rgba(30,30,63)` glass as the main surface.
- **StockSearchInput** on light surfaces: `tone="on-light"` or omit (default).
- **StockSearchInput** on unmigrated dark panels (workbench until P3.2): `tone="on-dark"`.
- **Never** `theme="dark"` on inputs — use `tone`, not Vuetify dark theme.
- **Never** `color="white"` as input text color.
- Use `design-tokens.css` (`--surface-bg`, `--text-primary`, `--field-fg`, …) on migrated pages; no raw `#e2e8f0` / `rgba(30,30,63)` on content cards.
- Do **not** change `App.vue` `.main-content` purple gradient to light gray (that would be full A, not A′).

